<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41094" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστρωφ-άω</span></b> , Frequentat. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστρέφω,</span> only intr., c. acc., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>visit</i> or <i>frequent</i> a
			place, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοὶ..ἐπιστρωφῶσι πόληας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.486
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέρος, ὅν τε θαμιναὶ
				ἐπιστρωφῶσι μέριμναι</span>
			<i>haunt</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				44
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαῖαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>A.</u>
					830
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς γῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phryn.Trag.
					5
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>go in and out of, frequent, haunt,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶμ᾽ ἐπιστρωφωμένου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					972
				</span></i>
			 ; also, <i>come to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόθεν γῆς τῆσδ᾽ ἐ. πέδον;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					666
				</span></i>
			.</div>
